leds: aw2013: don't write to the chip while it is powered off

When no LED is on, aw2013_brightness_set() powers the chip down (GCR = 0,
vcc and vio regulators off). A further brightness_set(LED_OFF) then still
writes the PWM and LCTR registers of the unpowered chip, which does not ACK:
the write fails with -ENXIO and the LED core logs "Setting an LED's
brightness failed (-6)". The pattern trigger (feedbackd) holds brightness 0
for part of every cycle, so on the Mi Max 2 this repeats every ~2.4 s.

The chip being off already means every LED is off, so return early.

Signed-off-by: Dimitris Vagiakakos <dimitrislinuxos@protonmail.ch>

--- a/drivers/leds/leds-aw2013.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-aw2013.c
@@ -163,6 +163,14 @@
 		ret = aw2013_chip_enable(led->chip);
 		if (ret)
 			goto error;
+	} else if (!led->chip->enabled) {
+		/*
+		 * The chip is powered off, so all LEDs are off already. Writing
+		 * to it would fail (no ACK without vcc), e.g. while the pattern
+		 * trigger holds brightness 0.
+		 */
+		ret = 0;
+		goto error;
 	}
 
 	num = led->num;
